Tangerines are a specific kind of mandarin orange.  Here in the US it
seems that clementines are more available as whole fruit (there's some
evidence that clementines may be a crossbreed between an older type and
a regular orange).

Usually when you get the canned mandarin oranges (that get thrown in
salads and cooked in gelatin desserts) they're from two other varieties
of mandarin orange: satsumas and mikans.  There are other less common
kinds as well.



